From 959a715299024e6f5822fc3d82373a3e90008f5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "keepup[bot]" <keepup[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: move OpenAI transcription to gpt-transcribe before
 whisper-1 shuts down

OpenAI announced on 26 Aug 2026 that whisper-1 shuts down on 26 Feb 2027 and
named gpt-transcribe as a successor. The OpenAI transcription provider hardcodes
whisper-1, so audio uploads through it would start failing that day.

- Default the provider to gpt-transcribe. OpenAI's transcription guide and API
  reference give it the same request and answer this provider already uses:
  file, model and temperature go in, and text comes back.
- Add a WhisperOpenAiModel setting (WHISPER_OPEN_AI_MODEL), added the same way
  as the generic provider's model, so the next change is a config edit and going
  back to whisper-1 until the shutdown is one too.
- When OpenAI refuses the configured model, name the model and the setting.
  Only OpenAI knows which models a key can use, and a list kept here would block
  the next model, so the check is OpenAI's answer rather than a list. A failure
  about the audio or another parameter keeps OpenAI's own message, even when it
  mentions the model, so it doesn't send anyone to the wrong setting.
- Replace the disabled "Whisper Large" field, which would now be wrong, with the
  real setting.

Replay date: 2026-09-01
Source: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/changelog (26 Aug entry)
